<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Collectivity of Saint Martin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as French Saint Martin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Collectivity of Saint Martin is the French northern part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> island of Saint Martin, whose southern part is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Sint Maarten. The division of the island dates from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-concordia">Treaty of Concordia</a> of 1648. Long a dependency of Guadeloupe, it became a separate French overseas collectivity in 2007, with its capital at Marigot, and lives mainly from tourism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/collectivity-of-saint-martin.jpg" alt="Collectivity of Saint Martin" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Martin_in_France.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
